1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Yuzuki

2
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Poor Yuzuki. She was crying.

3
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,000
They're only one building away from a Tetris.

4
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,000
And then the whole city might just disappear on us.

5
00:00:44,000 --> 00:01:04,000
If that does happen, I wonder if whatever's making Yuzuki sad will disappear too.

6
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Hey, Grandma, I'm finally…

7
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:23,000
About time.

8
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:29,000
We've been wondering when you were going to get home.

9
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Yuzuki was nice enough to help with dinner tonight, such an angel.

10
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:35,000
Not to mention a real whiz in the kitchen.

11
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Oh, stop it. You're embarrassing me.

12
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:39,000
What the what?

13
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:49,000
It's valid.

14
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Physics

15
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:59,000
We're in offerings come into finally a person.

16
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:02,000
The truth is, in the infinity holes in the mind.

17
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:05,000
We come into the show.

18
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:08,000
Federation-san, please, your father and hypocrite.

19
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:37,980
Thank you.

20
00:02:38,000 --> 00:03:07,980
Thank you.

21
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:10,000
Thank you.

22
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:39,000
So, Yuzuki...

23
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:43,180
Thanks to a belly full of food and a hot bath, now I'm all inner charge!

24
00:03:44,180 --> 00:03:45,340
Aurichalcum attack!

25
00:03:45,420 --> 00:03:45,720
No!

26
00:03:46,140 --> 00:03:47,860
Hey, cut it out!

27
00:03:48,060 --> 00:03:48,600
Take that!

28
00:03:48,980 --> 00:03:50,820
Please! That tickles, Yuzuki! Stop it!

29
00:03:51,060 --> 00:03:51,760
Quit it!

30
00:03:52,020 --> 00:03:52,780
Knock it off!

31
00:03:53,040 --> 00:03:53,620
Bad girl!

32
00:03:53,620 --> 00:03:57,560
Yeah, so I'm... I'm sorry.

33
00:03:58,780 --> 00:04:00,420
I was really mean to you.

34
00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:03,740
Why not?

35
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:06,220
Because I have no idea what you're thinking, Ruko!

36
00:04:07,200 --> 00:04:10,360
I don't know what she's thinking. It scares me.

37
00:04:12,100 --> 00:04:16,620
It's okay! No biggie. It's nothing to apologize for.

38
00:04:16,620 --> 00:04:23,100
The truth is, I was so afraid of losing to Akira the whole time.

39
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:28,120
I was upset, and then it just ended in the worst way.

40
00:04:28,520 --> 00:04:28,860
Oh.

41
00:04:29,660 --> 00:04:30,460
That's not all.

42
00:04:31,620 --> 00:04:33,140
There's this boy I like.

43
00:04:35,620 --> 00:04:36,060
But...

44
00:04:36,060 --> 00:04:37,980
We can never be together.

45
00:04:38,140 --> 00:04:38,320
What?

46
00:04:38,720 --> 00:04:40,600
Come on now, don't think like that.

47
00:04:41,020 --> 00:04:43,160
Hey, I'm sure this guy will fall for you.

48
00:04:44,180 --> 00:04:46,240
It won't happen.

49
00:04:46,820 --> 00:04:48,200
And it shouldn't either.

50
00:04:50,120 --> 00:04:51,200
I just wish...

51
00:04:52,480 --> 00:04:54,300
These feelings would go away.

52
00:04:58,660 --> 00:04:59,980
Hold on a sec.

53
00:05:00,460 --> 00:05:03,200
This guy you have a thing for, it's not...

54
00:05:03,200 --> 00:05:05,200
It's not...

55
00:05:05,200 --> 00:05:09,740
Time!

56
00:05:10,720 --> 00:05:12,840
Stop it, you tickle monster!

57
00:05:12,840 --> 00:05:32,820
I wonder what it feels like to be in love.

58
00:05:32,820 --> 00:05:35,520
I guess you get really excited, huh?

59
00:05:35,540 --> 00:05:36,440
Yeah, excited!

60
00:05:36,780 --> 00:05:38,420
You know what makes Tala excited?

61
00:05:38,660 --> 00:05:39,020
Battle!

62
00:05:39,020 --> 00:05:39,960
What?

63
00:05:41,700 --> 00:05:42,620
I love you, this girl!

64
00:05:43,340 --> 00:05:44,820
This girl...

65
00:05:45,640 --> 00:05:45,740
What?

66
00:05:45,800 --> 00:05:46,240
I like the cool...

67
00:05:46,240 --> 00:05:56,920
Kazuki?

68
00:06:16,240 --> 00:06:21,600
Oh, she went home already?

69
00:06:22,180 --> 00:06:23,320
Yeah, a while ago.

70
00:06:24,260 --> 00:06:26,400
Okay. Thanks so much.

71
00:06:27,920 --> 00:06:30,460
Hitue comes here to study and practice battle strategies.

72
00:06:30,940 --> 00:06:32,560
She takes notes and that seems to help her.

73
00:06:33,100 --> 00:06:35,340
So I figured it wouldn't hurt me to give it a shot.

74
00:06:35,540 --> 00:06:36,900
That's a fantastic idea.

75
00:06:37,820 --> 00:06:40,300
Bet you'll be kicking butt and taking names in no time.

76
00:06:40,300 --> 00:06:46,220
Hitue!

77
00:06:48,860 --> 00:06:52,360
And she's gone.

78
00:06:58,460 --> 00:07:04,180
So, I thought about it a whole lot.

79
00:07:05,180 --> 00:07:06,960
And my answer to you is yes.

80
00:07:06,960 --> 00:07:10,160
So let's be friends.

81
00:07:10,300 --> 00:07:11,440
Just like you asked.

82
00:07:11,720 --> 00:07:12,220
Is that okay?

83
00:07:16,860 --> 00:07:18,020
Of course it is!

84
00:07:19,220 --> 00:07:21,160
We're friends. It's official.

85
00:07:24,980 --> 00:07:25,840
Yuzuki, too!

86
00:07:26,400 --> 00:07:27,720
Well, if you're okay with it.

87
00:07:28,020 --> 00:07:28,680
Talking to me?

88
00:07:29,200 --> 00:07:30,280
Yeah, sure. Why not?

89
00:07:32,280 --> 00:07:34,140
Two friends at the same time?

90
00:07:34,140 --> 00:07:40,700
We cross is just so surprising.

91
00:07:40,700 --> 00:07:41,100
Huh?

92
00:07:41,500 --> 00:07:47,800
You see, during that battle I had with Akira, things got so painful I started to wonder if I'd ever even want to play again.

93
00:07:48,960 --> 00:07:50,200
Yeah, I know the feeling.

94
00:07:50,200 --> 00:07:54,400
I knew battling as a selector would probably hurt.

95
00:07:54,400 --> 00:07:56,440
But no pain, no gain, right?

96
00:07:56,760 --> 00:07:58,900
We are trying to fight for a wish, after all.

97
00:07:59,740 --> 00:08:04,460
Thing is, I enjoyed my battle with Ruko so much that it completely changed my tune.

98
00:08:04,960 --> 00:08:05,680
It was fun.

99
00:08:05,680 --> 00:08:06,600
Awesome!

100
00:08:06,840 --> 00:08:07,800
I had fun, too.

101
00:08:08,180 --> 00:08:11,000
Well, in that case, why don't we all play a round just for kicks?

102
00:08:11,220 --> 00:08:12,580
Yeah, that's a great idea.

103
00:08:12,840 --> 00:08:14,180
But we're all selectors.

104
00:08:14,380 --> 00:08:18,040
So if we battle against each other, that means somebody's wish could...

105
00:08:18,040 --> 00:08:19,580
Nah, don't worry about it.

106
00:08:19,840 --> 00:08:23,800
As long as none of our L-rigs are in the deck, we can play the game just like normal people do.

107
00:08:25,140 --> 00:08:25,580
Oh.

108
00:08:25,580 --> 00:08:32,520
All right, you guys wait here, okay?

109
00:08:33,640 --> 00:08:35,480
Take care, Hitu-e, and have fun.

110
00:08:35,980 --> 00:08:36,420
Thanks.

111
00:08:41,420 --> 00:08:42,440
All right, then.

112
00:08:43,380 --> 00:08:44,460
Your turn, Hitu-e.

113
00:08:44,620 --> 00:08:45,140
Let's go.

114
00:08:45,700 --> 00:08:46,060
Right.

115
00:08:47,400 --> 00:08:49,060
Man, when do I get to play?

116
00:08:49,120 --> 00:08:50,300
Did rock, paper, scissors.

117
00:08:50,720 --> 00:08:51,540
You're up next.

118
00:08:51,860 --> 00:08:52,320
Finally.

119
00:08:53,460 --> 00:08:55,240
Okay, summon Baromet.

120
00:08:55,480 --> 00:08:55,700
What?

121
00:08:57,180 --> 00:08:57,700
Wait.

122
00:08:58,460 --> 00:09:00,020
Yeah, let me see.

123
00:09:00,660 --> 00:09:02,920
Baromet's power level is only 7,000.

124
00:09:03,500 --> 00:09:08,260
So if Yusuke has her card grow on next turn, she'd crush it in one shot, right?

125
00:09:10,100 --> 00:09:11,180
Yeah, she would.

126
00:09:11,300 --> 00:09:13,100
Wait, I...

127
00:09:13,100 --> 00:09:16,900
Jeez, how would you like it if I gave away your strategies when you're playing?

128
00:09:17,360 --> 00:09:18,360
Oh, sorry.

129
00:09:21,800 --> 00:09:22,980
Tomo wants battle!

130
00:09:22,980 --> 00:09:26,580
You and Ruko are really alike, aren't you?

131
00:09:28,660 --> 00:09:31,300
Well, I guess Hitu-e's wish already came true.

132
00:09:32,160 --> 00:09:34,260
So she doesn't need to battle anymore.

133
00:09:34,820 --> 00:09:35,720
It seems not.

134
00:09:36,440 --> 00:09:37,520
You okay with that?

135
00:09:38,120 --> 00:09:38,680
I am.

136
00:09:38,680 --> 00:09:40,780
But that means you're...

137
00:09:40,780 --> 00:09:43,280
It's fine.

138
00:09:45,700 --> 00:09:46,580
No, wait!

139
00:09:46,720 --> 00:09:47,320
Not that one!

140
00:09:48,600 --> 00:09:49,160
Right.

141
00:09:50,040 --> 00:09:50,840
So sorry.

142
00:09:51,420 --> 00:09:52,920
Well, you are helping me.

143
00:09:53,320 --> 00:09:54,860
So there's no need to apologize.

144
00:09:55,720 --> 00:09:57,700
We're friends now, right, you big doofus?

145
00:09:57,700 --> 00:09:59,140
So...

146
00:09:59,140 --> 00:10:01,960
Friends tease and call each other names, huh?

147
00:10:02,140 --> 00:10:02,980
All the time!

148
00:10:03,240 --> 00:10:04,640
Try calling us something dumb.

149
00:10:04,880 --> 00:10:06,180
Like Stinky or Jerk.

150
00:10:06,880 --> 00:10:08,000
Just do it.

151
00:10:08,500 --> 00:10:09,840
It's not like we'll get mad.

152
00:10:10,620 --> 00:10:11,760
Um, okay.

153
00:10:12,520 --> 00:10:13,400
Well, here goes.

154
00:10:14,100 --> 00:10:15,260
Hi, Stinky.

155
00:10:15,920 --> 00:10:16,780
Hi, Jerk.

156
00:10:16,780 --> 00:10:25,300
I've never seen Hitu-e smile like that.

157
00:10:25,800 --> 00:10:29,060
I have to admit, I sometimes wish I wasn't her L-Rig.

158
00:10:29,760 --> 00:10:31,640
Well, there's no point in torturing yourself.

159
00:10:32,540 --> 00:10:33,640
I suppose not.

160
00:10:33,840 --> 00:10:34,860
Tama likes Roo!

161
00:10:35,640 --> 00:10:37,180
Likes Roo a whole lot!

162
00:10:37,480 --> 00:10:38,640
Likes being your L-Rig!

163
00:10:38,980 --> 00:10:39,560
Yay, Roo!

164
00:10:39,560 --> 00:10:40,760
Yes, but...

165
00:10:40,760 --> 00:10:41,520
It's okay.

166
00:10:42,680 --> 00:10:45,040
After all, Tama and Roo are friends.

167
00:10:46,720 --> 00:10:47,780
Wait a sec.

168
00:10:48,160 --> 00:10:49,200
You mean...

169
00:10:49,200 --> 00:10:49,680
Right.

170
00:10:50,460 --> 00:10:51,660
Tama doesn't know.

171
00:10:53,460 --> 00:10:54,540
I see.

172
00:10:56,340 --> 00:10:56,980
Yes!

173
00:10:57,200 --> 00:10:57,960
I'm next!

174
00:10:58,340 --> 00:11:00,700
Jeez, you really like me across, don't you?

175
00:11:02,060 --> 00:11:03,380
Yeah, I sure do.

176
00:11:03,480 --> 00:11:03,940
A lot!

177
00:11:09,560 --> 00:11:14,480
Yeah, I saw her out in the front!

178
00:11:14,900 --> 00:11:15,700
Oh, really?

179
00:11:16,100 --> 00:11:17,460
Yes, Akira's here!

180
00:11:17,720 --> 00:11:18,960
You mean the famous bottle?

181
00:11:19,400 --> 00:11:19,800
Uh-huh!

182
00:11:20,260 --> 00:11:22,400
Oh, I would love to see you at my hand.

183
00:11:22,940 --> 00:11:23,640
Oh, no!

184
00:11:24,200 --> 00:11:26,980
You're telling me Roo-Roo already went home for the day?

185
00:11:27,940 --> 00:11:29,040
That's so mean.

186
00:11:29,140 --> 00:11:30,780
She broke her promise to meet me.

187
00:11:31,080 --> 00:11:32,560
What a lousy thing to do.

188
00:11:33,160 --> 00:11:34,660
Yeah, tell me about it.

189
00:11:34,660 --> 00:11:36,220
How dare she stand you up?

190
00:11:36,260 --> 00:11:37,700
Do you want us to go make her sorry?

191
00:11:38,620 --> 00:11:39,100
Mm-mm.

192
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:42,000
I'm sure she had a real good reason.

193
00:11:42,680 --> 00:11:43,200
Oh, well.

194
00:11:43,500 --> 00:11:44,900
Just have to try tomorrow.

195
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:46,840
Oh, wait!

196
00:11:46,940 --> 00:11:49,280
What happens if she leaves before I get here again?

197
00:11:49,660 --> 00:11:51,920
I wish someone could keep tabs on her.

198
00:11:52,080 --> 00:11:54,880
But that's just crazy talk, because who would want to do that?

199
00:11:55,320 --> 00:11:56,480
Ooh, I'd be happy to.

200
00:11:56,500 --> 00:11:57,240
Yeah, me too.

201
00:11:57,540 --> 00:11:58,760
Leave it to us, okay?

202
00:11:58,760 --> 00:11:59,460
I'm so wonderful.

203
00:11:59,460 --> 00:12:01,780
I wonder where Tama's the life is.

204
00:12:01,780 --> 00:12:02,880
I think it's really tasty.

205
00:12:03,020 --> 00:12:05,100
Aw, thank you girls so much.

206
00:12:05,160 --> 00:12:07,260
I've got a shoot to get to, so Tama's.

207
00:12:07,260 --> 00:12:07,580
Yeah!

208
00:12:07,580 --> 00:12:22,200
I don't want to go home.

209
00:12:22,900 --> 00:12:25,780
You can't keep hiding from Kazuki like this forever.

210
00:12:25,780 --> 00:12:28,220
Yeah, I know, but...

211
00:12:28,220 --> 00:12:29,000
Yuzuki!

212
00:12:32,540 --> 00:12:33,340
It's Akira.

213
00:12:34,540 --> 00:12:36,240
She was at school this afternoon.

214
00:12:36,240 --> 00:12:41,840
Dang, Ruko, you won again.

215
00:12:42,200 --> 00:12:42,600
Booyah!

216
00:12:42,740 --> 00:12:44,300
That means you get me a milk tea.

217
00:12:44,640 --> 00:12:46,780
I'll take some sweet bean soup while you're up.

218
00:12:46,900 --> 00:12:47,500
Sure, Grandma.

219
00:12:48,280 --> 00:12:48,980
Oh, man.

220
00:12:49,220 --> 00:12:52,140
I lose a game, and all of a sudden, I'm you guys' personal waiter.

221
00:12:52,220 --> 00:12:53,100
Chop, chop, garçon!

222
00:12:53,100 --> 00:12:54,820
Yes, ma'am.

223
00:12:55,320 --> 00:12:56,800
Glad to see you're in better spirits.

224
00:12:56,880 --> 00:12:57,020
Huh?

225
00:12:58,200 --> 00:13:00,800
Well, are you ready for a game against me, Rue?

226
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:03,100
The loser will have to clean the bathroom.

227
00:13:03,380 --> 00:13:03,720
What?

228
00:13:04,020 --> 00:13:04,700
No way!

229
00:13:04,780 --> 00:13:05,660
You're too good!

230
00:13:06,960 --> 00:13:10,320
I like playing for fun against Grandma and Ayumu like this.

231
00:13:10,320 --> 00:13:20,380
But, to be honest, I like battling along with Tama even more.

232
00:13:21,380 --> 00:13:25,060
Not just for fun, but on a battlefield.

233
00:13:26,640 --> 00:13:29,100
In matches against other selectors.

234
00:13:30,840 --> 00:13:32,100
It's weird, though.

235
00:13:32,760 --> 00:13:35,840
In those battles, everyone's fighting so hard for their wishes.

236
00:13:35,840 --> 00:13:41,800
And even though I don't have one, I want to keep fighting harder, too.

237
00:13:42,520 --> 00:13:43,320
What's that, dear?

238
00:13:43,940 --> 00:13:45,120
Oh, I'm sorry.

239
00:13:45,720 --> 00:13:46,680
It's my turn, right?

240
00:13:53,480 --> 00:13:54,960
Aki was looking for me?

241
00:13:55,640 --> 00:13:56,080
Yeah.

242
00:13:56,460 --> 00:13:59,260
She must want to battle against you pretty bad, Rukov.

243
00:13:59,520 --> 00:14:01,340
That stalker just doesn't give up.

244
00:14:01,820 --> 00:14:05,200
Yeah, but I don't even have a wish like the other selectors do.

245
00:14:05,840 --> 00:14:09,300
So, I guess there wouldn't be any harm in fighting her then, would there?

246
00:14:09,720 --> 00:14:10,640
No, you're wrong!

247
00:14:11,020 --> 00:14:13,740
Whatever you do, please don't battle Akira, okay?

248
00:14:14,660 --> 00:14:15,800
Um, sure.

249
00:14:17,880 --> 00:14:18,280
Listen.

250
00:14:18,840 --> 00:14:22,120
She's gonna do anything to get you to fight, but you just have to ignore her.

251
00:14:22,580 --> 00:14:24,640
She might even try to turn your friends against you.

252
00:14:26,040 --> 00:14:28,200
Oh, I'm not worried about that.

253
00:14:28,520 --> 00:14:30,700
It's just you and Hitoi, and I trust you guys.

254
00:14:33,160 --> 00:14:33,480
Ruru!

255
00:14:33,480 --> 00:14:36,580
So glad you're finally here.

256
00:14:36,820 --> 00:14:37,860
Yeah, I'll say.

257
00:14:38,360 --> 00:14:39,240
So what up, girlfriend?

258
00:14:39,740 --> 00:14:39,980
Huh?

259
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:41,940
Oh, guess what?

260
00:14:41,980 --> 00:14:44,320
We all just got a really cool text from Akira.

261
00:14:44,720 --> 00:14:48,220
She's got a shoot this afternoon, and she said we can come if we bring you.

262
00:14:48,540 --> 00:14:51,260
She'll give us a tour of the studio if we all go together.

263
00:14:52,260 --> 00:14:54,640
There's a chance we might get to meet Iona, too.

264
00:14:54,760 --> 00:14:55,140
Sorry.

265
00:14:55,740 --> 00:14:57,900
Appreciate the offer, but we've already got plans.

266
00:14:58,020 --> 00:14:59,860
You weren't invited, so shut your face!

267
00:14:59,860 --> 00:15:00,280
What?

268
00:15:00,780 --> 00:15:01,660
Come on, Ruru.

269
00:15:01,980 --> 00:15:03,020
Come with us.

270
00:15:03,760 --> 00:15:04,960
Um, but I...

271
00:15:05,800 --> 00:15:06,800
Watch yourself.

272
00:15:07,960 --> 00:15:12,000
There is no stronger bond of friendship than a mutual enemy, Frankfurt Moore.

273
00:15:12,280 --> 00:15:12,800
All right.

274
00:15:13,240 --> 00:15:14,640
That's about it for today, class.

275
00:15:14,860 --> 00:15:15,960
Tomorrow we'll start with...

276
00:15:15,960 --> 00:15:18,320
Ruku, time to go.

277
00:15:19,140 --> 00:15:19,660
Yusuki?

278
00:15:20,580 --> 00:15:21,820
Talk about rude.

279
00:15:22,300 --> 00:15:26,440
Where do you get off barging your way in here and ordering our friend around like that?

280
00:15:26,660 --> 00:15:27,740
She's not your friend.

281
00:15:28,200 --> 00:15:28,440
Ruku?

282
00:15:30,060 --> 00:15:30,580
Coming!

283
00:15:32,380 --> 00:15:33,900
You're going with us!

284
00:15:33,900 --> 00:15:35,360
Hey, what's all this about?

285
00:15:35,700 --> 00:15:38,080
You stay out of it, stubbleface.

286
00:15:38,240 --> 00:15:38,480
What?

287
00:15:39,140 --> 00:15:39,740
Stubbleface?

288
00:15:39,740 --> 00:15:47,920
After them!

289
00:15:48,200 --> 00:15:49,680
And send out a text to everybody!

290
00:15:52,880 --> 00:15:54,220
I've spotted them!

291
00:15:56,820 --> 00:15:57,460
Go!

292
00:15:57,940 --> 00:15:59,360
Move it, you jerk!

293
00:16:01,780 --> 00:16:02,720
Over here!

294
00:16:02,920 --> 00:16:03,180
Right!

295
00:16:03,180 --> 00:16:03,240
Right!

296
00:16:03,240 --> 00:16:17,080
Oh, I really want to hang out with Akira.

297
00:16:17,320 --> 00:16:17,560
No!

298
00:16:18,040 --> 00:16:18,780
Yusuki, look.

299
00:16:18,980 --> 00:16:19,600
It's okay.

300
00:16:20,460 --> 00:16:22,320
It's no big deal if I gotta battle her.

301
00:16:25,120 --> 00:16:26,280
But it is.

302
00:16:26,520 --> 00:16:27,580
Let me put it this way.

303
00:16:28,100 --> 00:16:30,340
Remember when I said I wish I knew what you were thinking?

304
00:16:30,720 --> 00:16:31,100
Yeah.

305
00:16:31,900 --> 00:16:32,800
Still do.

306
00:16:33,680 --> 00:16:36,360
But there is one thing I know for certain about you.

307
00:16:37,520 --> 00:16:39,420
You really like Wee Cross battles.

308
00:16:39,940 --> 00:16:41,280
You're so happy when you play.

309
00:16:44,780 --> 00:16:46,700
But battling Akira is awful.

310
00:16:47,440 --> 00:16:48,120
It's painful.

311
00:16:49,700 --> 00:16:51,420
Trust me, I know from experience.

312
00:16:52,100 --> 00:16:54,640
And I'm worried that playing her will make you hate the game.

313
00:16:56,640 --> 00:16:58,100
I don't want that to happen.

314
00:16:58,840 --> 00:16:59,280
Yusuki.

315
00:17:03,240 --> 00:17:04,320
Down this way?

316
00:17:04,700 --> 00:17:06,100
That's what the first year said.

317
00:17:06,860 --> 00:17:07,940
This isn't good.

318
00:17:08,460 --> 00:17:10,380
I'll draw them outside and distract them.

319
00:17:10,660 --> 00:17:12,100
So you just stay put, okay?

320
00:17:13,060 --> 00:17:13,620
No.

321
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:14,520
Wait.

322
00:17:14,980 --> 00:17:15,900
Hey, don't worry.

323
00:17:16,500 --> 00:17:17,240
Be back soon.

324
00:17:17,840 --> 00:17:18,060
What?

325
00:17:22,240 --> 00:17:23,320
Here they are!

326
00:17:23,540 --> 00:17:24,680
Don't let them get away!

327
00:17:24,680 --> 00:17:37,180
Dang it all.

328
00:17:37,180 --> 00:17:40,900
I'm grateful to have a friend who's so worried about me.

329
00:17:40,900 --> 00:17:42,280
But the truth is...

330
00:17:42,280 --> 00:17:46,640
It's better if she doesn't know.

331
00:17:47,260 --> 00:17:48,960
And I can't even explain it.

332
00:17:49,820 --> 00:17:52,440
But I still want to do this for some reason.

333
00:17:53,100 --> 00:17:53,920
Am I nuts?

334
00:17:53,920 --> 00:17:56,880
Why do I want to battle Akira so bad?

335
00:17:57,300 --> 00:17:58,840
It's all I can think about.

336
00:17:59,000 --> 00:17:59,340
Ruu!

337
00:18:02,920 --> 00:18:04,920
Ruu and Tama are the same!

338
00:18:05,300 --> 00:18:06,880
Want to battle Akira too!

339
00:18:10,760 --> 00:18:12,800
There's something scary about her.

340
00:18:12,800 --> 00:18:16,180
But she and I...

341
00:18:16,180 --> 00:18:17,960
We're the same.

342
00:18:18,940 --> 00:18:20,080
She's frightening.

343
00:18:21,860 --> 00:18:23,860
I don't know what Ruko's thinking.

344
00:18:24,760 --> 00:18:25,800
There's something...

345
00:18:26,360 --> 00:18:28,020
Scary about her.

346
00:18:28,760 --> 00:18:30,020
That's not true!

347
00:18:30,020 --> 00:18:30,100
No!

348
00:18:34,140 --> 00:18:34,820
Hey!

349
00:18:34,820 --> 00:18:43,500
Ruu-Ruu.

350
00:18:43,780 --> 00:18:45,200
Come out and play.

351
00:18:49,700 --> 00:18:51,180
Guess who's here?

352
00:18:51,420 --> 00:18:51,840
Whoa!

353
00:18:51,940 --> 00:18:52,860
Awesome sauce!

354
00:18:53,120 --> 00:18:53,500
Ladies!

355
00:18:53,840 --> 00:18:55,180
Thank you so much!

356
00:18:55,440 --> 00:18:56,820
You asked and we delivered!

357
00:18:57,060 --> 00:18:58,960
You are the best up top!

358
00:19:02,300 --> 00:19:03,420
Well, Ruu-Ruu?

359
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:04,360
Let's go!

360
00:19:05,820 --> 00:19:06,840
Um, Akira?

361
00:19:07,120 --> 00:19:08,140
What about us?

362
00:19:10,200 --> 00:19:11,420
Yeah, I've got to shoot.

363
00:19:11,540 --> 00:19:12,140
Get lost.

364
00:19:13,140 --> 00:19:16,120
But I thought you said we could hang out with you.

365
00:19:16,600 --> 00:19:19,200
A top model like me hanging with a bunch of uggos?

366
00:19:19,920 --> 00:19:20,780
Not likely.

367
00:19:20,780 --> 00:19:21,680
Mm-mm.

368
00:19:31,460 --> 00:19:33,760
No one's gonna bother us in here, Ruu-Ruu.

369
00:19:33,760 --> 00:19:35,500
So you're ready to throw down?

370
00:19:35,500 --> 00:19:36,440
Or what?

371
00:19:36,440 --> 00:19:37,440
No one's gonna bother us in here, Ruu-Ruu.

372
00:19:39,440 --> 00:19:40,260
This is it.

373
00:19:40,640 --> 00:19:42,200
I'm gonna play against Akira.

374
00:19:47,820 --> 00:19:48,200
Hey.

375
00:19:48,200 --> 00:19:52,220
If you're looking for a battle, give me a shot.

376
00:19:57,220 --> 00:19:57,820
That's...

377
00:19:57,820 --> 00:19:59,000
Damn it!

378
00:19:59,160 --> 00:20:00,400
You skank-ass hoes!

379
00:20:00,460 --> 00:20:01,900
Stop trying to steal my opponents!

380
00:20:02,460 --> 00:20:03,420
You misunderstand.

381
00:20:03,880 --> 00:20:04,960
I'm challenging you.

382
00:20:05,040 --> 00:20:05,440
What?

383
00:20:05,440 --> 00:20:09,620
It seems you only like to prey on rookies.

384
00:20:10,440 --> 00:20:11,940
Guess you're just scared of me.

385
00:20:14,440 --> 00:20:14,920
Akira!

386
00:20:15,460 --> 00:20:15,680
Huh?

387
00:20:16,060 --> 00:20:17,720
I've been looking all over for you.

388
00:20:17,980 --> 00:20:18,980
Come on, you're up.

389
00:20:18,980 --> 00:20:22,920
No, wait, I, um, I need a few minutes, okay?

390
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:24,240
We don't have a few minutes.

391
00:20:24,280 --> 00:20:24,560
No!

392
00:20:24,820 --> 00:20:25,700
Stop shoving!

393
00:20:25,800 --> 00:20:26,380
It won't take long, I swear!

394
00:20:26,380 --> 00:20:28,360
We've got a whole crew waiting on you, so get the lead out.

395
00:20:28,360 --> 00:20:39,540
Um, thanks for that great fake-out.

396
00:20:40,040 --> 00:20:40,880
What fake-out?

397
00:20:41,400 --> 00:20:42,560
I was serious.

398
00:20:42,900 --> 00:20:43,140
Huh?

399
00:20:44,080 --> 00:20:45,920
You wanted to have a battle, didn't you?

400
00:20:45,920 --> 00:20:46,420
Uh...

401
00:20:46,420 --> 00:20:48,980
Perhaps you had a grudge with Akira.

402
00:20:50,040 --> 00:20:50,780
No, wait.

403
00:20:51,500 --> 00:20:52,480
That's not it.

404
00:20:53,400 --> 00:20:54,680
You'll battle anybody.

405
00:20:56,040 --> 00:20:57,680
Anything to get your fix.

406
00:20:58,360 --> 00:20:59,020
Am I right?

407
00:21:06,700 --> 00:21:07,660
I am right.

408
00:21:09,880 --> 00:21:10,780
So battle me.

409
00:21:19,580 --> 00:21:20,340
Wait a minute.

410
00:21:22,720 --> 00:21:23,780
You have no wish.

411
00:21:28,360 --> 00:21:35,620
Participating as a selector without having a wish is more than just wrong.

412
00:21:38,880 --> 00:21:40,160
It's blasphemy.

413
00:21:41,520 --> 00:21:43,340
That won't go unpunished.

414
00:21:43,340 --> 00:21:43,940
Wait.

415
00:21:51,940 --> 00:21:52,500
Blasphemy?

416
00:21:52,500 --> 00:22:18,060
You have no wish.

417
00:22:18,060 --> 00:22:24,100
今日の祈りは明日多分になる

418
00:22:24,100 --> 00:22:29,960
天と地を映す逆さまの名誉

419
00:22:29,960 --> 00:22:35,960
回りだした歯車

420
00:22:35,960 --> 00:22:42,020
人混みの中で耳を澄ましたら

421
00:22:42,020 --> 00:22:47,620
魂を召くあの鈴の音

422
00:22:47,620 --> 00:23:17,600
Thank you.

423
00:23:17,620 --> 00:23:26,460
A WeCross party?

424
00:23:26,800 --> 00:23:29,160
I might even find another selector to battle.

425
00:23:29,220 --> 00:23:30,820
All this time, I never noticed.

426
00:23:31,260 --> 00:23:33,800
I just can't get my hair tied up right, that's all.

427
00:23:33,820 --> 00:23:35,460
I don't want to hear you talk like that ever again.

428
00:23:35,460 --> 00:23:36,700
She was also kind of scary.

429
00:23:37,520 --> 00:23:39,600
Next time, that invalidated vow.

